-The host in this container is dsh **0.1.2-alpha.2**.
+- **Bundle mount.** `package.json` declares `dsh.bundle.patch`, and
+  `cordis.patch.yml` inserts the `bench-status` row, so installing the package
+  mounts the plugin without a hand-written profile row.
+- **Job-registry read.** The count behind the status route is read through the
+  official background-job registry: `inject` is `['jobs']` and the count is
+  `ctx.jobs.list().length` (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs`, provided in-tree by
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs-local`). The read is caller-relative, so from the
+  plugin's unscoped host-plane context it covers unowned jobs, and a settled
+  unowned job stays listed until the registry is disposed.
+- **`/bench-status/status` HTTP route.** An `exact` route registered through the
+  official web carrier interface `ctx.webServer.register`
+  (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-webserver`), answering
+  `{"ok":true,"open":<count>}`. The carrier is optional: on a composition that
+  mounts no HTTP server (the headless bundle) the plugin still activates and
+  serves no route.
+- **Job-completion subscription.** Each settled job is logged from the official
+  registry listener `ctx.jobs.onJobDone` (the pre-0812 `onTaskDone` spelling).
 
